name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-lesson9-cfu_2026'
title 'Check for Understanding'

wrong 'The condition is missing a semicolon.'
wrong 'The function `awardBadge()` should be in quotes.'
right 'There is no bug — the code works as described.'
wrong 'The operator should be `&&` instead of `||`. As written, the badge is given if either is true, not both.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

markdown <<MARKDOWN
A fitness app should award a "Hydration Hero" badge when a user has logged a workout AND drunk 8 glasses of water. The code says:

```
if (loggedWorkout || drankWater) {
    awardBadge();
}
```

What is the bug?
MARKDOWN
